{"title":"Career Roadmap · Design Researcher","role":"Design Researcher","summary":"A Design Researcher studies people, behaviours, environments, needs and systems to generate evidence that guides product and service design. In healthcare and medical product design, the role focuses on understanding patients, caregivers, clinicians and healthcare workflows and translating those insights into better products, services and experiences.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Design Researcher studies people, behaviours, environments, needs and systems to generate evidence that guides product and service design. In healthcare and medical product design, the role focuses on understanding patients, caregivers, clinicians and healthcare workflows and translating those insights into better products, services and experiences."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Healthcare / Medical Product Design","Research Projects","Design Research Internship","Junior Design Researcher / UX Researcher","Design Researcher","Senior Researcher","Research Lead / Design Strategy Lead"]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Design Researcher” is a broad career rather than a regulated healthcare profession. A B.Des can provide a strong entry route, particularly into healthcare UX research, medical-product research, human factors, service design and design strategy. Clinical research, biomedical research and regulated medical-device roles may require additional specialised qualifications."}]},{"heading":"What Does a Design Researcher Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A design researcher investigates what people need, how they behave, what problems they face and why existing solutions fail."},{"type":"p","text":"In healthcare, research subjects can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patients"},{"text":"Doctors"},{"text":"Nurses"},{"text":"Surgeons"},{"text":"Technicians"},{"text":"Caregivers"},{"text":"Hospital administrators"},{"text":"Pharmacists"},{"text":"Laboratory staff"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conduct user interviews"},{"text":"Observe users in real environments"},{"text":"Perform contextual research"},{"text":"Create user personas"},{"text":"Map user journeys"},{"text":"Analyse qualitative data"},{"text":"Identify pain points"},{"text":"Conduct usability studies"},{"text":"Study healthcare workflows"},{"text":"Analyse competing products"},{"text":"Convert findings into design requirements"},{"text":"Present research insights to design and engineering teams"},{"text":"Validate design concepts with users"}]},{"type":"h","text":"The central question is:"},{"type":"h","text":"“What evidence should guide the design decision?”"}]},{"heading":"Why Healthcare / Medical Product Design Fits","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Relevance"],"rows":[[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Healthcare workflows"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Product design"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Design strategy"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Data interpretation"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Medical-device knowledge"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Medium"}],[{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"High"}]]},{"type":"flow","items":["A strong candidate combines design thinking","research methodology","healthcare understanding."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Research & Design Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Interview techniques"},{"text":"Human behaviour"},{"text":"Psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Design research methods"},{"text":"Information organisation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research methods"},{"type":"h","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Desk research"},{"text":"Competitive analysis"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Diary studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Clinics"},{"text":"Diagnostic centres"},{"text":"Pharmacies"},{"text":"Patient journeys"},{"text":"Healthcare professionals"},{"text":"Medical products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Study a simple healthcare problem such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"“Why do patients struggle to understand prescription instructions?”"},{"type":"h","text":"Conduct:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observation","Interviews","Analysis","Insights","Design Recommendations"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Human-Centred Research"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should develop more rigorous research skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"User personas"},{"text":"Journey mapping"},{"text":"Service blueprints"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"User segmentation"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare research"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient journeys"},{"text":"Clinical workflows"},{"text":"Medical-device interaction"},{"text":"Hospital environments"},{"text":"Medication-management problems"},{"text":"Elderly users"},{"text":"Users with disabilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Major project"},{"type":"h","text":"Research a healthcare workflow such as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient","Registration","Consultation","Diagnosis","Payment","Pharmacy"]},{"type":"h","text":"Identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Delays"},{"text":"Confusion"},{"text":"Communication gaps"},{"text":"Accessibility issues"},{"text":"Emotional pain points"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Healthcare Research"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the stage to move from academic research toward professional research."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced interview techniques"},{"text":"Research planning"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Healthcare service design"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Evidence-based design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start using research tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Survey platforms"},{"text":"Statistical tools"},{"text":"Qualitative-analysis tools where available"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship targets"},{"type":"h","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare design consultancies"},{"text":"Medical-device companies"},{"text":"Health-tech startups"},{"text":"Hospitals with innovation teams"},{"text":"UX research teams"},{"text":"Healthcare product companies"},{"text":"Service-design consultancies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Specialisation & Professional Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should demonstrate the ability to conduct complete research projects."},{"type":"h","text":"Capstone workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Question"},{"type":"h","text":"Stakeholder Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Interviews / Observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Data Collection"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Insights"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Prototype / Design Direction"},{"type":"h","text":"User Validation"},{"type":"h","text":"Final Recommendations"},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio should contain"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objectives"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Participant profiles"},{"text":"Interview guides"},{"text":"Observation notes"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Affinity maps"},{"text":"Personas"},{"text":"Journey maps"},{"text":"Research insights"},{"text":"Design recommendations"},{"text":"Validation results"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not show only the final product."},{"type":"p","text":"For a research portfolio, the reasoning and evidence are the product."}]},{"heading":"Design Research Process","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional design researcher typically follows:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Define"},{"type":"p","text":"What exactly are we trying to understand?"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Recruit"},{"type":"p","text":"Who needs to participate?"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct interviews, observation, surveys or usability studies."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Analyse"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify patterns and contradictions."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Synthesize"},{"type":"p","text":"Convert raw observations into insights."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Recommend"},{"type":"p","text":"Translate insights into design opportunities."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Validate"},{"type":"p","text":"Test whether the proposed direction actually addresses the problem."}]},{"heading":"Research Methods to Master","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Ethnographic observation"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Usability testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Basic experimental design"},{"text":"Data interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Secondary research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Competitive analysis"},{"text":"Market research"},{"text":"Existing clinical evidence"},{"text":"Industry reports"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest researchers know when to use each method rather than applying the same method to every problem."}]},{"heading":"Healthcare-Specific Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A design researcher in healthcare should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anxiety"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Health literacy"},{"text":"Waiting"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Privacy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospital workflows"},{"text":"Consultation"},{"text":"Diagnosis"},{"text":"Treatment"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Discharge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Medical products"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Cleaning"},{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Error prevention"},{"text":"Human-machine interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Users"},{"type":"h","text":"Always consider multiple stakeholders:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient"},{"type":"h","text":"↕"},{"type":"h","text":"Caregiver"},{"type":"h","text":"↕"},{"type":"h","text":"Doctor / Nurse"},{"type":"h","text":"↕"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital"},{"type":"h","text":"↕"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturer"},{"type":"p","text":"A product that works well for one stakeholder may create problems for another."}]},{"heading":"Human Factors & Usability","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is an especially valuable specialisation."},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human error"},{"text":"Cognitive load"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Physical interaction"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Safety-critical interfaces"},{"text":"Error prevention"},{"text":"User feedback"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example, a medical-device interface should not merely look attractive."},{"type":"h","text":"The researcher should ask:"},{"type":"p","text":"Can the user understand the information correctly under pressure?"}]},{"heading":"Research Ethics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Healthcare research requires strong ethical awareness."},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Participant privacy"},{"text":"Confidentiality"},{"text":"Sensitive information"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Vulnerable participants"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Institutional approval where applicable"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Never collect or expose unnecessary patient-identifying information in a student research project."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"College research projects"},{"text":"Design research clubs"},{"text":"Academic research assistance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX research internships"},{"text":"Service-design internships"},{"text":"Health-tech projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical-device companies"},{"text":"Healthcare startups"},{"text":"Healthcare UX teams"},{"text":"Design consultancies"},{"text":"Hospital innovation teams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4"},{"type":"h","text":"Seek:"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Design Research Intern → Junior Researcher"}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Patient Journey Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Research:"},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency Department Patient Experience"},{"type":"h","text":"Map:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Arrival","Registration","Waiting","Consultation","Testing","Treatment","Discharge"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Medical Device Usability"},{"type":"p","text":"Study how users interact with a non-invasive healthcare device."},{"type":"h","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Setup"},{"text":"Controls"},{"text":"Instructions"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Errors"},{"text":"Cleaning"},{"text":"Storage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Elderly Healthcare Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Study challenges faced by elderly users when navigating healthcare services."},{"type":"h","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Digital literacy"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Caregiver involvement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Medication Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Research why patients miss or misunderstand medication instructions."},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research findings"},{"text":"User journey"},{"text":"Pain points"},{"text":"Design requirements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Hospital Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"Research one operational workflow and identify opportunities for improvement."},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates systems thinking, which is highly valuable in healthcare design."}]},{"heading":"Research Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to produce professional research deliverables."},{"type":"h","text":"Research plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Problem"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Objectives"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Questions"},{"type":"h","text":"Participants"},{"type":"h","text":"Methods"},{"type":"h","text":"Timeline"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Research report"},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Executive summary"},{"text":"Background"},{"text":"Methodology"},{"text":"Participants"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Insights"},{"text":"Opportunities"},{"text":"Recommendations"},{"text":"Limitations"}]}]},{"heading":"Tools & Software","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research & collaboration"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Google Workspace"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Adobe Creative Cloud"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Basic Python"},{"text":"Basic statistical tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Surveys"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Typeform"},{"text":"Qualtrics where available"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Presentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PowerPoint"},{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Adobe InDesign"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The tool is secondary. Research quality and reasoning are the primary skills."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX research"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Service design"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Healthcare design"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Healthcare innovation"},{"text":"Accessibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, a certificate is useful only when it is accompanied by demonstrable research work."}]},{"heading":"Interview Questions","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is design research?"},{"text":"What is the difference between qualitative and quantitative research?"},{"text":"How would you conduct a user interview?"},{"text":"How do you avoid leading questions?"},{"text":"What is contextual inquiry?"},{"text":"What is affinity mapping?"},{"text":"What is a user journey map?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How would you research a medical device?"},{"text":"How would you study a hospital workflow?"},{"text":"How would you research elderly patients?"},{"text":"How would you handle sensitive participant information?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Scenario"},{"type":"p","text":"Doctors say a medical device is easy to use, but patients repeatedly make errors. What would you do?"},{"type":"h","text":"Strong approach:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observe Actual Use","Identify User Differences","Analyse Errors","Test Assumptions","Conduct Usability Study","Identify Root Cause","Recommend Changes"]}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Possible postgraduate directions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Design Research"},{"text":"M.Des Interaction Design"},{"text":"M.Des Industrial Design"},{"text":"M.Des Service Design"},{"text":"MA Design Research"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Healthcare Design"},{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Service Innovation"},{"text":"Design Strategy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For healthcare-specific research, additional study in human factors, healthcare systems, biomedical design or health informatics can strengthen the profile."}]},{"heading":"Related Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"This background can lead to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Researcher"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"Healthcare UX Researcher"},{"text":"Human Factors Researcher"},{"text":"Service Designer"},{"text":"Healthcare Service Designer"},{"text":"Design Strategist"},{"text":"Product Researcher"},{"text":"User Researcher"},{"text":"Design Consultant"},{"text":"Innovation Researcher"},{"text":"Experience Researcher"},{"text":"Research Lead"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Design Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI is changing research workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"Useful applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Research summarisation"},{"text":"Qualitative coding assistance"},{"text":"Pattern identification"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Persona exploration"},{"text":"Literature discovery"},{"text":"Synthetic concept testing"},{"text":"User-behaviour analysis"},{"text":"Research repository search"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI-generated summaries should not replace direct engagement with participants or critical interpretation of evidence."},{"type":"h","text":"The researcher must still determine:"},{"type":"p","text":"What does the evidence actually mean?"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Experience","Typical Role"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Design / UX Researcher"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Design Researcher"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Design Researcher"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Research Lead"}],[{"text":"10–15 years"},{"text":"Design Strategy / Research Manager"}],[{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Head of Research / Design Strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Interviewing","Observation","Surveys","Usability Testing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"flow","items":["Qualitative Coding","Statistics","Synthesis","Insight Generation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Journey","Clinical Workflow","Human Factors","Accessibility"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"flow","items":["Service Design","Product Design","UX","Prototyping"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Communication","Presentation","Stakeholder Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI-Assisted Research","Data Analysis","Digital Health","Responsible AI"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"B.Des Healthcare / Medical Product Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"UX / Healthcare Research Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Design Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Design Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Strategy / Research Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Head of Research / Design Strategy"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal B.Des Healthcare / Medical Product Design → Design Researcher candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"🔎 3–4 complete research projects"},{"text":"🧑‍⚕️ Understanding of healthcare stakeholders"},{"text":"🏥 Knowledge of basic healthcare workflows"},{"text":"🗣️ Strong user-interview skills"},{"text":"👁️ Observation and contextual-research skills"},{"text":"📊 Basic quantitative research and statistics"},{"text":"🧩 Qualitative analysis and synthesis"},{"text":"🧭 Journey mapping and service-design skills"},{"text":"🧪 Usability-testing experience"},{"text":"⚕️ Human factors and accessibility knowledge"},{"text":"🔐 Research ethics and privacy awareness"},{"text":"📑 Professional research reports"},{"text":"💻 Figma/Miro + research/data tools"},{"text":"🏢 At least one relevant research or healthcare internship"},{"text":"🤖 Awareness of AI-assisted research workflows"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Ideal graduate profile","text":"“A human-centred researcher who can investigate real healthcare problems, collect and analyse evidence, translate findings into actionable design opportunities, and communicate those insights clearly to multidisciplinary product teams.”"}]}]}